========

So the main concept your trainer is teaching is:

Frontend (HTML) → Flask Backend (main.py) → ML Model (.pkl) → Prediction → Backend → Frontend

This is specifically a Flask Machine Learning web application workflow.

This Flask ML workflow is complete once the backend validates the submitted values before 
passing them to model.pkl for prediction and rendering the result in index.html, which prevents invalid input from reaching the model.

=======

| Step | File / Component | Action                          |
| ---- | ---------------- | ------------------------------- |
| 1    | `index.html`     | User enters input               |
| 2    | `main.py`        | Flask receives the request      |
| 3    | `model.pkl`      | ML model processes the input    |
| 4    | `main.py`        | Gets the prediction result      |
| 5    | `index.html`     | Displays the result to the user |


=======

Flow:

User → index.html → main.py → model.pkl → main.py → index.html → User

The table identifies each Flask ML component, and 
the request flow can be mapped to a complete main.py example so the files work together in practice.

=========

| File / Folder | Type                   | Purpose                                                                                                               |
| ------------- | ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `main.py`     | Python Backend         | Main Flask application. Handles requests, user input, ML model processing, and sends the result back to the frontend. |
| `model.pkl`   | Machine Learning Model | Stores the trained ML model and is used to make predictions.                                                          |
| `templates/`  | Folder                 | Contains HTML files used for the frontend.                                                                            |
| `index.html`  | HTML Frontend          | Displays the user interface, accepts user input, and shows the prediction result.                                     |
| `static/`     | Folder                 | Contains static frontend files.                                                                                       |
| `style.css`   | CSS                    | Controls the design, colors, layout, and appearance of the website.                                                   |


==========




